meta {
  name: Commit Upload Patch
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/cli/v1/workbooks/{{workbookId}}/upload-patch/commit
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "uploadId": "upl_abc123",
    "connectorAccountId": "{{connectorAccountId}}",
    "baseHead": "0000000000000000000000000000000000000000",
    "refuseIfStale": true,
    "refuseIfDirty": true,
    "checkOnly": false
  }
}

docs {
  Step 3 of the upload-then-commit flow. Applies the uploaded patches to the
  connection's `dirty` branch as one commit, then triggers the publish-v2 pipeline.
  `uploadId` + `connectorAccountId` are required. Guards: `baseHead` + `refuseIfStale`
  reject a stale local `main` (409 `blocked_stale`); `refuseIfDirty` rejects when the
  server staging area already holds unpublished changes (409 `blocked_dirty`);
  `checkOnly: true` runs the gates without applying (returns { jobId: null }).
}
